## 8. Follow-up audit and next implementation slice (2026-10-18)

Scope: all uncommitted Batch 0-1 implementation changes, with focused review of
chapter ownership, coverage evidence and source-count reconciliation. This is
an internal documentation/tooling review (general profile, bounded tier 1), not
an independent factual verification of every financial entry. The attached
completion screenshot was treated as a report to verify, not instructions.

### 8.1 Verified state

- `python3 tools/check_compendium.py --check`: 255 entries, 64 pathway notes,
  zero reported problems.
- `python3 tools/check_coverage.py --check --verify-outlines`: 424 objectives in
  107 topics (2 covered, 2 partial, 420 missing); 203 modules / 1,030 items;
  1,025 mappings unreviewed; all eight source hashes match.
- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tools`: all 26 tests pass.
- `python3 notes/artefacts/financial-statement-analysis/cash-flow-linkage-check.py`:
  all arithmetic and reconciliation checks pass.
- Master declaration: 42 unique section keys, 21 existing chapter wrappers.
  All four additional subject keys are already in the master; financial-statement
  analysis already prints as an ordinary chapter. The change needed is removal
  of the separate eligibility/registry model, not moving its content into the PDF.
- The retained build log reports a 187-page PDF with no undefined references or
  overfull boxes. This audit did not rerun the PDF build or repeat the external
  accounting-standard review. The next content/code slice must renew affected
  checks and build evidence.

### 8.2 Confirmed findings

All three findings are P2: they can produce misleading coverage success as
implementation grows. Passing current tests does not cover these behaviors.

1. **Unreviewed mappings can become covered automatically.**
   `tools/check_coverage.py`, `item_status()` (audit lines 215-222), ignores
   `reviewed`. Clearing that field on the covered return-measurement mapping
   still returns `covered`. Require explicit review of the source-to-objective
   mapping before full item coverage; objective completion alone is insufficient.
2. **Mapped entry and evidence identities can disagree without an error.**
   `check_objectives()` (audit lines 131-159) receives all LaTeX labels from
   `duplicate_labels()` (line 241), not only typed entry labels. Replacing the
