## 12. Tooling standardisation: Python 3.14, uv and make (executed 2026-10-18)

The repository's Python tooling now follows the conventions of the maintainer's
research repository. No compendium content, coverage status or source record
changed in substance.

**Environment.** `.python-version` pins Python 3.14.7. `pyproject.toml` pins uv
0.12.7 (`required-version`) and exact runtime versions: NumPy 2.4.6, SciPy 1.18.1
and statsmodels 0.15.0, with pandas 3.0.5 as a constraint. The `dev` group (default)
holds pytest 9.1.1, ruff 0.16.5, pre-commit 4.6.2 and pre-commit-hooks 6.0.0; the
`empirical` group holds openpyxl 3.1.5 and xlrd 2.0.2 for the spreadsheet scripts.
`uv.lock` resolves them; the project is not a package (`package = false`).

**Targets.** `make sync`; `make source-check` (lock check, ruff lint, ruff format
check, both checkers, pytest and every `notes/artefacts/*/*check*.py` script under
`-W error`); `make check` (adds `verify-outlines` and `pdf`); `make pre-commit`.
CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs `make source-check` on Python 3.14.7 when a pull
request into `main` is labelled `ready-to-merge`. It needs a `GUIDE_READ_TOKEN` secret
to check out the private guide submodule. The outline hashes and the PDF need
git-ignored local copies, so they run locally only.

**Lint and format.** Ruff uses the reference configuration (py314, 100 columns,
E/F/I/W/UP/RUF/D/ANN401, Google docstrings, labelled import groups). Evidence scripts
are exempt from line length, docstring presence and form (D1, D205, D403), lambda
assignment and short names (E731, E741), because their docstrings record sources and
their names follow the cited formulas. Preserved `superseded-*` runs are excluded
from ruff and the hooks (`--force-exclude`) so they stay byte-identical to HEAD.

**Code changes required by the new versions.** `np.trapz` (removed in NumPy 2.4)
became `np.trapezoid` in two scripts; two scripts cast NumPy scalars with `float()`
so their printed output keeps its earlier form; `adfuller` is called with
`result_object=False` to avoid a statsmodels FutureWarning. Run lines and interpreter
notes now name `uv run python` (`uv run --group empirical python` for spreadsheet
inputs).

**Verification.** All 55 check scripts pass under 3.14.7 with warnings as errors.
Their printed output matches the earlier Anaconda Python 3.11 run (NumPy 1.26.4,
SciPy 1.13.1) except for three cosmetic differences: a 1e-18 rounding residue in
`liquidity-market-design-checks.py`, a printed `-0.` in `black-litterman-check.py`
and the version line of `inference-simulation-checks.py`, whose output otherwise
matches the recorded Python 3.10.16 run exactly. After ruff formatting, the outputs
of all 55 scripts are byte-identical to their pre-format output. The data-dependent
empirical scripts were not rerun; their syntax trees were compared with HEAD instead,
and every difference (removed unused imports, docstring layout, the edits above) was
reviewed. Whitespace hooks trimmed trailing spaces and final newlines in
`strategystructure.tikz` and three `notes/tooling/*.tex` files.

