### 19.1 Correction pass on PR #24 (executed 2026-10-18)

A fixes-only pass on draft PR #24 at `88bd29e`, after an external audit with six
findings. No objective was added. This pass is exempt from the 30-objective target
(Section 17.4), which stands for future expansion prompts.

1. **Discrete-dividend replication** (`meth:equity-forward-futures-valuation`). Borrowing
   S0 - I left the share purchase unfunded by I = 2.940743. The replication now borrows
   the full 100 and applies each dividend to the loan, leaving a debt of 101.020320 at
   maturity. A dated cash-flow ledger replaces the circular check.
2. **Equity swap** (`meth:swap-valuation-replication`). The next equity payment is worth
   N(E_t/E_0 - P(t,T_next)), 7.980133 million in the example (N(E_t/E_0 - 1) would give
   6.000 million).
   - It is separated from the later payments, the whole leg and the net value.
   - An equity-for-SOFR leg with realised overnight growth gives a net value of
     N(E_t/E_0 - A_t).
   - Checks cover the reset and payment-date limits and a stochastic-rate simulation.
   - Hull's p. 778 expression is documented as a discrepancy. His Technical Note 19, read
     from an archived copy because the author's site returns 404, supports the
     correction.
3. **Treasury noncompetitive limit** (`def:government-agency-supranational-funding`).
   The limit is $10 million from 8 August 2022 under 31 CFR 356.12 and 356.22; the
   Handbook's $5 million is historical. The October 2026 amendment leaves the limit
   unchanged, and the 35 percent cap is stated as the competitive rule.
4. **SOFR FRN** (`meth:floating-money-market-yields`). The FRN has a dated schedule, and
   SOFR is compounded on business days with calendar-day weights, as in the New York Fed
   methodology.
   - Discounting is consistent with the projection, so the note is at par at its quoted
     margin.
   - The discount margin is 96.38 bp (was 96.4).
   - Accrual, index and round-trip checks were added.
5. **SOFR futures hedge** (`meth:rate-bond-forward-valuation`). The SOFR + 200 bp
   borrowing and the quarter-year accrual are restored. The hedge is derived from rates
   and locks 2.01 percent in both scenarios.
6. **Duration equivalence** (`meth:curve-based-empirical-duration`). The two measures are
   equal only on a flat curve or for a single cash flow. Counterexample: parallel-zero
   duration 10.218587 against yield duration 11.213091.

Checks rose from 163 to 189 (bond valuation 89, forward and swap 64, term structure 36).
Five source keys and reading notes were added: `cfr-31-356-auction-limits`,
`fr-2022-13409`, `fr-2026-21069`, `hull-tn19` and `nyfed-sofr-averages-index`. The
seven objectives and ten outline items mapped to the corrected entries were reassessed
and remain covered. Totals are unchanged: 101 of 424 objectives; 125 Level I, 31 Level
II and 37 shared-core items covered; 837 of 1,030 unreviewed. Details are in
`notes/source-review-records.md`, *Correction pass on PR #24*. Remote CI was not
triggered.

### 19.2 Second correction pass on PR #24 (executed 2026-10-19)

A fixes-only pass on draft PR #24 at `642e29c`, after an audit that confirmed the six
corrections of Section 19.1 and found three further issues. No objective was added and none
was newly completed; the pass is exempt from the batch target (Section 17.4).

1. **Bond forward schedule** (`meth:rate-bond-forward-valuation`). The original example
   (accrued interest 0.90 now and 0.375 at delivery, a coupon in 0.35 years, delivery in
   0.50 years) fitted no regular semiannual calendar. It now uses one dated schedule:
   - a 5 percent note with coupons on 15 May and 15 November, accrued actual/actual in
     period on the scheduled dates (Hull, sec. 6.1, pp. 152-153);
   - the Sunday 15 November 2026 coupon is paid on Monday 16 November without extra
     interest (31 CFR 356.30(a));
   - spot trade on 16 October 2026, settling T+1 on 19 October; delivery on 19 April 2027;
     term repo at 4.20 percent, simple act/360.

   Accrued interest is 2.133152 (157 of 184 days) at spot and 2.140884 (155 of 181) at
   delivery. The full spot price is 103.333152, the coupon PV 2.491860, the forward full
   price 102.982489 and the quoted forward 100.841605. Independent checks: a coupon
   calendar generated back from maturity, a two-repo dated ledger with zero net cash
   before delivery, and the carry identity (quoted forward - spot quote = financing
   2.194107 - coupon income 2.507732 - interest on the paid coupon 0.044770). The later
   value of the long is 0.395798.
2. **Municipal discount** (`rule:bond-issuance-legal-tax`). "The exemption covers coupon
   interest only" is replaced, from IRS Publication 550 (2025) and Publication 1212
   (December 2025):
   - a holder's share of original-issue discount on a qualifying tax-exempt bond is
     tax-exempt interest, accrued by constant yield and added to basis;
   - market discount is not exempt and is ordinary income for purchases after 30 April
     1993, unless it is below the de minimis amount (the earlier text had the direction
     reversed);
   - other price changes are capital gains or losses against the adjusted basis.

   A worked example compares a holder at issue (basis 918.58 after five years, capital
   loss 68.58 on a sale at 850) with a secondary buyer at 850 (market discount 68.58 above
   the 37.50 de minimis amount, exempt OID 81.42, ordinary gain 68.58 at redemption).
   The Handbook's statement (chap. 9, p. 221) and its reversed market-discount sign
   (p. 223) are recorded as discrepancies.
3. **Check counts.** At `642e29c` the scripts executed 90 bond, 64 forward-and-swap and 36
   term-structure checks, 190 in all. Section 19.1 and the review record reported 89 and
   189, one fewer than the bond script executes; the record does not show how 89 was
   counted. The convention is now stated in both script
   docstrings: one check is one executed `ok()` call, so a call in a loop counts once per
   iteration. After this pass the counts are 94, 69 and 36, a total of 199.
4. **Batch preference.** Section 17.4 now asks for 45 newly completed objectives per
   expansion prompt. The earlier 30-objective batches keep their records.

Three source keys and reading notes were added: `cfr-31-356-30-payment-dates`,
`irs-pub-550-2025` and `irs-pub-1212-2025`. Three objectives were reassessed against
the corrected teaching and remain covered: `explain-bond-legal-tax-factors`,
`value-rate-and-bond-forwards` and `value-forward-contracts`. So were their
corrected outline items (`outline:7099c7688942:m052:b02`,
`outline:0242f4b7ba07:m031:b04`), which carry re-review notes. The other items
mapped to these objectives are unaffected by the changed passages.

Totals are unchanged: 101 of 424 objectives; 125 Level I, 31 Level II and 37 shared-core
items covered; 837 of 1,030 unreviewed. Details are in `notes/source-review-records.md`,
*Second correction pass on PR #24*. Remote CI was not triggered.

